Place the T-shaped piece \(D\) in the open central gap: its vertical stroke occupies the 4th column in rows 3–5, and its middle crossbar extends left across row 4.  

With this addition:
- the plus shape \(B\) has no valid center left;
- the straight 5-cell bar \(C\) cannot fit in any available column/row;
- every possible location of the U-shape \(A\) meets an occupied square;
- every possible location of the P-shape \(E\) meets an occupied square.

Thus the only choice that blocks all the other four shapes is \(D\).

\[
\boxed{\text{D}}
\]
